Happy early birthday to your husband! Here is what I found for Friday 11 September.

**Availability**
- The Warehouse tasting tour at 14:30 has 11 places left, so there is room for the two of you. It is for ages 18 and over.
- If you would like something earlier, the Classic tour at 11:00 has 4 places.

**Accessibility**
- The shop, cafe and still house all have step-free access and a lift.
- The warehouse floor is uneven. That matters for the warehouse tasting tour, and I don't have more detail on how the tour route handles it for wheelchair users. I'd suggest contacting the visitor centre before you book so they can tell you whether the tour will work for him. He could also decide on the day, depending on how he's feeling.

**Parking**
- There is free parking for cars beside the visitor centre. I don't have information on designated accessible bays or which spaces are closest to the entrance. The car park is right next to the building, so you won't have far to go. The team can confirm the best spot when you speak to them.

I can also check the cafe hours if you'd like to plan a bite before or after the tour.
